# Canonical walk_2d viewer/CTest demo: single-family sparse 2-D locomotion space.
# Four logically-similar walking anchors (no cross-family jog), so every
# within-hull blend interpolates similar poses -- the parametric-synthesis
# precondition the PMG paper assumes. A dissimilar gait (jog) belongs in a
# separate node joined by a transition edge, not blended into this space; the
# cross-family case is preserved as a stress fixture at
# specs/fixtures/fixture_walk_2d_jog_crossfamily.pmg_spec.
#
# Axis 0 (turn_rate):    wide -> tight walk turn.
# Axis 1 (travel_speed): authored support reaches ~0.75 via walkStraightTwiceAsFast.
# The old [0,1] jog corner is intentionally dropped -- it was the cross-family
# jolt source, not a usable walking speed -- so the speed support is smaller than
# a full rectangle. Requests beyond the hull project onto the authored triangles.
# See docs/audits/jolt-cross-family-diagnosis-20260623.md.
#
# Loop seam: each anchor references one explicit foot-strike-aligned cycle window
# (start_frame/end_frame), chosen by --extract-candidate-windows to minimize the
# last->first-frame seam. registration declares cycle_joint LeftAnkle so
# --audit-cyclic-continuity reports the loop seam for this node; with explicit
# windows the builder uses them verbatim (no auto cycle re-detection). Pose loop
# seam dropped from ~2.7x to ~0.2-0.5x the median in-clip step; the residual
# weak_yaw_rate flag is natural intra-stride turn-rate variation (and near-zero
# sign wobble for the straight walk), not a pose pop. walkTightCurve keeps its
# hand-authored window (its per-cycle heading delta exceeds the extractor filter).
# See docs/audits/walk-2d-loop-seam-recut-20260623.md.

node walk_2d 2
registration walk_2d LeftAnkle - 3 0
parameter_metrics walk_2d turn_rate travel_speed
parameter_calibration walk_2d 5
parameter_support walk_2d triangulated_2d

example walk_2d -0.3 0.0 ../BVH/walkMoreCurve.bvh start_frame 1 end_frame 34
example walk_2d  0.0 0.0 ../BVH/walkCurve.bvh start_frame 127 end_frame 160
example walk_2d  1.0 0.0 ../BVH/walkTightCurve.bvh start_frame 33 end_frame 67 phase_label left_contact_start contact_start L=contact;R=swing contact_end L=contact;R=swing
example walk_2d  0.15 0.75 ../BVH/walkStraightTwiceAsFast.bvh start_frame 27 end_frame 60

triangle walk_2d 0 1 3
triangle walk_2d 1 2 3

expect walk_2d spanned_axes 2

edge walk_2d walk_2d
edge_phase_range walk_2d walk_2d 0.70 0.95 0.05 0.30
edge_config walk_2d walk_2d 120 234 3 6 41
